A THIRD SLOT WAS ADDED, and it was earned under -race: 0x0F38 counts collections ENTERED, set before
runtime.GC() rather than after. The vacuity check first read `collected`, which counts COMPLETIONS — so a
guest that died INSIDE the first collection scored 0 and was reported as having exercised nothing, when
dying inside a collection is the not-stopped world biting hardest. Un-raced the negative arm dies after one
collection completes; under -race it dies inside the first.
